.TH CERTWATCHER 1 "2026-05-15" "certwatcher 1.4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
certwatcher \- SSL/TLS certificate monitoring tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B certwatcher
[\fIoptions\fR] \fIhost\fR [\fIhost2\fR ...]
.br
.B certwatcher
[\fIoptions\fR] \fB\-f\fR \fIhostfile\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B certwatcher
checks SSL/TLS certificates on remote hosts and reports their status,
expiry dates, chain validity, and cryptographic details.
.PP
Designed for sysadmins, DevOps engineers, and security teams who need
to monitor certificate expiry across many hosts.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-p " port"
Port to connect to (default: 443).
.TP
.BI \-t " seconds"
Connection timeout in seconds (default: 10).
.TP
.BI \-w " days"
Warning threshold in days (default: 30). Certificates expiring within
this many days are flagged.
.TP
.BI \-f " file"
Read hostnames from file, one per line. Lines starting with # are comments.
.TP
.BI \-s " name"
Override the SNI (Server Name Indication) hostname sent during TLS handshake.
.TP
.B \-v
Verbose output. Show IP address, SANs, serial number, fingerprint, and
full certificate chain.
.TP
.B \-1
One-line output per host. Compact format for dashboards.
.TP
.B \-q, \-\-quiet
Suppress all output. Only exit codes are used.
.TP
.B \-\-csv
Output in CSV format.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output in JSON format.
.TP
.B \-\-pem
Output certificates in PEM format.
.TP
.BI \-o " file"
Write output to file instead of stdout.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable colored output.
.TP
.B \-\-expired\-only
Only show certificates that are expired or expiring within the warning threshold.
.TP
.B \-\-exit\-warn
Exit with code 1 if any certificate is expiring within the warning threshold.
.TP
.B \-\-sort
Sort results by days until expiry (ascending).
.TP
.B \-\-match\-host
Flag hostname mismatches as warnings.
.TP
.BI \-\-starttls " protocol"
Perform STARTTLS negotiation before TLS handshake. Supported protocols:
smtp, imap, ftp.
.TP
.B \-\-brief
Compact status overview: hostname, status (OK/WARN/EXPIRED/ERROR), and days remaining.
.TP
.B \-\-fingerprint
Print only the SHA256 fingerprint for each host.
.TP
.B \-\-issuer\-only
Print only the issuer for each host.
.TP
.B \-\-san\-list
Print all Subject Alternative Names for each host.
.TP
.B \-\-ndjson
Newline-delimited JSON output (one object per host).
.TP
.B \-\-version\-json
Print version as JSON.
.TP
.B \-\-color=\fImode\fR
Color mode: always, never, or auto (default).
.TP
.B \-\-chain
Display certificate chain hierarchy.
.TP
.B \-\-expiry\-date
Print raw expiry date per host.
.TP
.B \-\-subject\-only
Print certificate subject per host.
.TP
.B \-\-cipher\-only
Print TLS version and cipher details per host.
.TP
.B \-\-serial\-only
Print certificate serial number per host.
.TP
.B \-\-key\-only
Print public key type and size per host.
.TP
.B \-\-ocsp\-only
Print OCSP stapling status per host.
.TP
.B \-\-timing\-only
Print connection timing breakdown (TCP, TLS, total) per host.
.TP
.B \-\-sig\-algo
Print signature algorithm per host.
.TP
.B \-\-self\-signed\-only
Only show self-signed certificates.
.TP
.B \-\-weak
Only show certificates with weak crypto (TLS < 1.2, small key sizes).
.TP
.B \-\-starttls xmpp
XMPP STARTTLS protocol support (port 5222).
.TP
.B \-\-starttls ldap
LDAP STARTTLS protocol support (port 389).
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Show version and exit.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show usage information and exit.
.SH EXIT CODES
.TP
.B 0
All certificates valid.
.TP
.B 1
At least one certificate expiring within threshold (with \-\-exit\-warn).
.TP
.B 2
Connection error occurred.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Check certificates for multiple hosts:
.PP
.RS
certwatcher google.com github.com cloudflare.com
.RE
.PP
Check with 14-day warning threshold, one-line output:
.PP
.RS
certwatcher \-w 14 \-1 \-f hosts.txt
.RE
.PP
JSON output for automation:
.PP
.RS
certwatcher \-\-json example.com | jq .
.RE
.PP
Check SMTP server certificate:
.PP
.RS
certwatcher \-\-starttls smtp \-p 25 mail.example.com
.RE
.PP
Silent check for monitoring scripts:
.PP
.RS
certwatcher \-q \-\-exit\-warn \-w 14 \-f hosts.txt || send\-alert
.RE
